From e5c5b7735439e40eb8ed6522174bc9a760c99c5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Morris <jmorris@namei.org>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 19:25:23 -0700
Subject: [RFC PATCH] riscv: dts: spacemit: k3-com260: keep dldo4 enabled

dldo4 on the P1 PMIC is marked regulator-boot-on, but has no consumer
described in the device tree.  The regulator core can therefore disable
the firmware-enabled rail during unused-regulator cleanup.

Reproduce the resulting failure on a K3 CoM260 IFX using the current
SpacemiT for-next tree plus the local K3 PCIe enablement needed for NVMe
and the RTL8852BE endpoint.

Without this change, dldo4 was disabled at 31.857578 seconds.  CPU1
hard-locked at 44.017326 seconds, the other CPUs stalled in
smp_call_function_many_cond() from TLB-flush paths, and RCU reported a
stalled grace-period thread.

In a matched test with the same source, configuration, toolchain, PCIe
graph, boot arguments, and root filesystem, adding only
regulator-always-on kept dldo4 enabled.  NVMe and RTL8852BE remained
active, and the system was healthy at 302.45 seconds with no lockup,
RCU-stall, panic, or Oops report.  This is one boot, not a long-term
stability claim.

The actual hardware consumer is not documented.  Describing that supply
relationship would be preferable; preserve the firmware state until it
is known.

All other regulator-boot-on rails in this PMIC block are also marked
regulator-always-on; dldo4 is the sole exception.  This RFC asks whether
dldo4 supplies an undocumented K3 or PCIe dependency and whether a supply
relationship should be described instead.

The same dldo4 description is present on K3 Pico-ITX, but that board was
not tested and is not changed here.  Do not route this RFC to stable yet:
the reproducer requires K3 PCIe enablement that is not in released
mainline kernels.

GitHub Copilot assisted with diagnosis, build and test automation, and
changelog drafting.

Fixes: cfe5c91cb73c ("riscv: dts: spacemit: k3: Initial support for CoM260-IFX board")
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k3-com260.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k3-com260.dtsi b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k3-com260.dtsi
index 92dea8639779..054bfff7413a 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k3-com260.dtsi
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/spacemit/k3-com260.dtsi
@@ -187,6 +187,7 @@ dldo3: dldo3 {
 			dldo4: dldo4 {
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <1800000>;
 				regulator-max-microvolt = <1800000>;
+				regulator-always-on;
 				regulator-boot-on;
 			};
 

